# The walker audit (arc.h): every site that reads a path by verb or element, with a disposition.
# One line per group of sites: library|file|symbols|disposition|reason|test
# Dispositions: updated, confirmed, unreachable, support, A2, owner (tools/check-verb-walkers.sh says what each means).
# The test is library:path:Suite.Name (a test that feeds the site an arc), "-" for a support file, "A2" for a pending site.
shape-geometry|src/path/path.c|gshgeom_path_element,gshgeom_path_bounds,gshgeom_path_hash,gshgeom_path_dump,gshgeom_path_copy,gshgeom_path_verb_points,gshgeom_path_verb_weights|updated|the element refuses an arc (AR15), bounds take the pieces (AR10), hash and dump spell the record (AR15), copy reproduces it, the verb tables know it (AR1)|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.PathElementBoundsHashDumpCopyEqualAndVerbKnowTheArc
shape-geometry|src/path/path.c|gshgeom_path_move_to,gshgeom_path_line_to,gshgeom_path_quadratic_to,gshgeom_path_cubic_to,gshgeom_path_rational_quadratic_to,gshgeom_path_rational_cubic_to,gshgeom_path_close,gshgeom_path_element_count|unreachable|the builders append their own verb and the element count counts elements; an arc is appended only by gshgeom_path_append_arc, and counts as one (AR16)|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.ElementCountCountsAnArcOnce
shape-geometry|src/path/arc.c|append_checked,gshgeom_path_arc,gshgeom_path_lower_arcs|updated|the arc record itself: validation, readback, and the lowering that replaces every arc by its pieces (AR2, AR8, AR15)|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.PathElementBoundsHashDumpCopyEqualAndVerbKnowTheArc
shape-geometry|src/path/vertices.c|read_seg,element,gshgeom_path_vertices,gshgeom_path_vertex_count|confirmed|phase 1: an arc is refused with ERR_UNSUPPORTED, passed on from the readback; AR14 gives it one vertex at its end|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.VerticesRefuseAnArcUntilItReadsOne
shape-geometry|src/along/along.c|gshgeom_measured_create|confirmed|phase 1: an arc is refused with ERR_UNSUPPORTED, passed on from the readback; AR12 measures its pieces|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.MeasuredCreateRefusesAnArcAndMeasuresTheLoweredPath
shape-geometry|src/stroke/expand.c|read_centerline,build_clip,build_clip_curves|confirmed|phase 1: an arc is refused with ERR_UNSUPPORTED before any outline is made; AR13 gives it a body of its pieces|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.StrokeExpansionRefusesAnArcSolidOrDashed
shape-geometry|src/stroke/dash.c|gshgeom_sk_dash_begin|confirmed|phase 1: reached only after the centerline has been read, which refuses an arc; AR13 cuts its pieces|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.StrokeExpansionRefusesAnArcSolidOrDashed
shape-geometry|src/stroke_curves/lower.c|gshgeom_stroke_curves_lower_cubic|confirmed|phase 1: an arc is refused with ERR_UNSUPPORTED; the lowering takes the pieces of gshgeom_path_lower_arcs (AR8)|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.StrokeCurvesLowerRefusesAnArc
shape-geometry|src/device/device.c|convert_element,gshgeom_device_path_from_model|confirmed|phase 1: an arc is refused with ERR_UNSUPPORTED; the conic route of CV1 lowers it to pieces first|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.DevicePathFromModelAndFlattenRefuseAnArc
shape-geometry|src/flatten/flatten.c|gshgeom_path_flatten|unreachable|reaches a path only through gshgeom_device_path_from_model, which refuses an arc|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.DevicePathFromModelAndFlattenRefuseAnArc
shape-cpu|src/render/sink.c|expansion_work|confirmed|counts elements only (gshgeom_path_element_count); an arc is one element (AR16)|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.ElementCountCountsAnArcOnce
shape-cpu|src/render/stroke.c|gshcpu_render_stroke_open|confirmed|counts elements only (gshgeom_path_element_count); an arc is one element (AR16)|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.ElementCountCountsAnArcOnce
shape-cpu|src/render/geometry.c|*|owner|reaches a path through gshgeom_device_path_from_model, which refuses an arc; the error is reported as ERR_LIMIT here (any error but OOM is), loud but misnamed: the sink owner updates it with the conic route|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.DevicePathFromModelAndFlattenRefuseAnArc
shape-scene|src/resource/resource.c|gshscene_path_equal,verb_points,verb_weights,build_path,gshscene_store_intern_path,replay|A2|reads a path through gshgeom_path_element: an arc is refused (the readback fails and from_geometry reports an internal error, loud but misnamed); A2 interns it with gshgeom_path_copy and gshgeom_path_equal|A2
shape-scene|src/glyph/glyph.c|append_element,append_outline,map_element|A2|reads an outline through gshgeom_path_element: an arc is refused; A2 maps it with gshgeom_arc_map (singular via pieces)|A2
shape-scene|src/resource/image_paint.c|path_quad|A2|the rectangle predicate reads five elements: an arc makes the readback fail and the predicate false, as a curve does; A2 states it|A2
vector|src/codec/svg/lower/lower_marker.c|gvec_lw_markers|confirmed|reads vertices through gshgeom_path_vertices, which refuses an arc until AR14 (the call fails and the lowering reports an internal error); no change in vector once it reads one|shape-geometry:tests/unit/test_walkers.cpp:Walkers.VerticesRefuseAnArcUntilItReadsOne
